bration foundation.\n- Chunk 4, pp. 10–12: full grader examples allow aliases, minor typos, numeric rounding and inferred units. Partial answers require semantic grading: an incomplete definitive answer and an explicitly acknowledged partial answer can differ. Never replace rubric with exact string matching. A/B/C output maps to CORRECT/INCORRECT/NOT_ATTEMPTED.\n- Chunk 5, p. 13: F = 2c/(2c+2i+a), where a is not-attempted count and all cases are scored. Confidence elicitation is a distinct intervention and is excluded from the fixed-suffix experiment.\n\n'\"''')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"/net/spaces/chenhao/chai-lab-models/haokunliu/safety/workspaces/simpleqa-factual-errors-versus-e11f-codex-gpt-6-astra\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
